## 🔮 Future Milestone 3.5: Remaster-Style Single-Screen UI

> Long-term target after the current side-by-side hybrid. The goal is a native
> PC UI that replaces the DS bottom screen entirely, not a copy of it.

### Layout/UX direction (PMD DX reference)

- **This is a layout remaster first, not an art replacement.** Keep the original PMD art language, fonts and icons initially; redesign how they are arranged for PC.
- **One 16:9 view.** No permanent DS bottom screen. Gameplay, HUD and menus all live on the single widescreen surface.
- **Gameplay HUD:** party HP/belly/level for leader + partner in the corners, floor/weather near the top centre, minimap as a toggleable corner panel, mission objective/status along the bottom edge.
- **Menus are full-screen or large modal panels**, not a second DS screen. Tabs/sections: Team, Bag, Moves, Dungeon Map, Options.
- **Controller-first navigation**, with mouse hover/click and keyboard support. Menus should remember focus and close with Cancel.
- **Touch-only flows** (rescue codes, names, touch grid) become on-screen keyboard/panel flows.
- **Keep the original readability hierarchy:** HP/belly first, floor/weather second, minimap/team third.
- Motion stays restrained: panel slides/fades and focus easing; no busy animations during battle.
- **HD art/icons come later**, after the layout and interaction model are proven.

### Architecture

- `runtime/ui/remaster_ui.*`: retained-mode UI model, navigation graph, focus/animation clock, screen stack.
- `runtime/ui/ui_renderer.*`: software ARGB8888 draw list into the presented framebuffer (rounded rects, gradients, borders, shadows, alpha, text, icon atlas).
- `runtime/ui/guest_ui_state.*`: read-only PMD Sky state bridge (party, HP/belly/level, floor, weather, mission, minimap, menu/selection state) using `pmdsky-debug` offsets.
- Input router: controller-first navigation plus keyboard/mouse hover/click. Guest input injection only where a host screen must drive an existing guest menu.
- Text: bundled open font rendered through `stb_truetype` (already available in the vendored ImGui tree), with a pixel-font option for authentic labels.
- Icons/art: texture atlas loaded from `runtime/ui/assets/`; keep original assets out of Git if they are ROM-derived.

### Phased plan

- [~] **3.5.0 Layout/input foundation**: first-pass draw list, 5x7 text, panel/bar/minimap drawing exists in `runtime/ui/remaster_hud.*`, but it is disabled in-game because the first style pass was not faithful enough. Focus/navigation graph and faithful panel/font work still pending.
- [~] **3.5.1 Gameplay HUD layout**: first pass read live party/weather and drew generic panels, but it covered the original menus and did not match PMD's panel language. Reverted to the faithful original bottom-screen side panel. Next pass must reproduce the original blue rounded panels, font, location banner, party/money/weather/play-time block, and menu cursor before replacing the side panel.
- [ ] **3.5.2 Pause/team menu layout**: full-screen pause and team panels; party status, moves, items, tactics, leader switching.
- [ ] **3.5.3 Main menu layout**: New Game / Continue / Options / Mods / Credits, with save-slot summaries.
- [ ] **3.5.4 Bag/inventory/moves layout**: item use/give/drop, move learning/reordering, IQ skills.
- [ ] **3.5.5 Touch replacement layout**: on-screen keyboard for rescue codes/names, touch-grid replacement, rescue mail flows.
- [ ] **3.5.6 HD art pass**: redraw fonts/icons/panels at high resolution, theme polish, motion.
- [ ] **3.5.7 Platform polish**: transitions, ultrawide/4:3 layouts, accessibility, localization hooks.

### Current state / fallback

- The current single-screen mode is a **side-by-side hybrid** (top widescreen left, bottom screen right when needed). It is a temporary bridge, not the final UI.
- First remaster HUD vertical slice lives in `runtime/ui/remaster_hud.*` and `runtime/ui/guest_ui_state.*`; the data bridge works, but the generic panel drawing is disabled in-game pending a faithful PMD-style pass.
- Single-screen hybrid uses a main screen plus a small side-column inset. During normal dungeon gameplay: top screen main, bottom map/status inset. When a top-screen menu window or team menu/touch grid is active: **bottom screen main**, top screen inset. This keeps the dungeon/menu view primary and the Controls page secondary.
- The inset sits in its own side column, not over the main view, so it does not obscure important content.
- Guest menu detection reads `WINDOW_LIST` active top-screen windows plus `display_data::team_menu_or_grid`.
- Default remains stacked dual-screen; side-by-side/corner layouts are opt-in.
- True widescreen uses the GPU2D adaptive text-BG compositor, with the width chosen from the saved aspect ratio at launch.
- In-game aspect changes are saved immediately and applied on the next launch.
- 120 Hz frame interpolation is active when the display reports ≥100 Hz. The title bar still reports the game's ~60 Hz logic rate, not the present rate.

